        "name": "whatsappTrigger",
        "type": "WhatsAppTrigger",
        "baseClasses": [
          "WhatsAppTrigger",
          "triggers",
          "json",
          "string"
        ],
        "category": "Triggers",
        "description": "Real-time WhatsApp Business Cloud API trigger — auto-answers customer WhatsApp messages via Meta Graph API",
        "inputParams": [
          {
            "label": "Phone Number ID (Optional)",
            "name": "phoneNumberId",
            "type": "string",
            "placeholder": "e.g. 109823475628109",
            "description": "Optional: Filter incoming messages for a specific Meta Phone Number ID.",
            "optional": true,
            "id": "whatsappTrigger_0-input-phoneNumberId-string"
          },
          {
            "label": "How to Use",
            "name": "howToUse",
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "optional": true,
            "additionalParams": true,
            "hint": {
              "label": "Setup Guide",
              "value": "\n## 🟢 WhatsApp Business Cloud API Setup & Token Guide\n\n### Step 1: Get Phone Number ID & Token\n1. Go to [Meta Developer Portal](https://developers.facebook.com) ➔ Your App ➔ **WhatsApp** ➔ **API Setup**.\n2. Copy your **Phone Number ID** into the **Phone Number ID** field below.\n3. Copy your **Temporary Access Token** (or System User Token) into the **Access Token** field below.\n\n### Step 2: Set Meta Webhook Callback URL\n1. Copy the Webhook URL from the top of this node (`https://core.aimicromind.com/webhook/{chatflowId}/whatsapp`).\n2. In Meta Developer Portal ➔ **WhatsApp** ➔ **Configuration** ➔ click **Edit Callback URL**.\n3. Paste the Webhook URL and enter your **Verify Token** (e.g. `my_whatsapp_token`).\n4. Click **Verify and Save** ✅.\n5. Subscribe to `messages`.\n\n### Step 3: Activate & Test Live\n1. Toggle the workflow to **ACTIVE** in the canvas header!\n2. Send a WhatsApp text to your test number — AI will auto-reply in real-time!\n"
            },
            "description": "Open \"Additional Parameters\" to see the setup guide.",
            "id": "whatsappTrigger_0-input-howToUse-string"
          }
        ],
